{"shortDescription":"Central European bond yields stabilised on Wednesday after rising to multi-year highs, tracking moves in core markets, as investors braced for U.S. Federal Reserve's interest rate decision later in the day.","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Central European bond yields stabilised on Wednesday after rising to multi-year highs, tracking moves in core markets, as investors braced for U.S. Federal Reserve's interest rate decision later in the day."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Markets have largely priced in a quarter-point rate increase by the Fed, which would lift its target range to 3.75%-4%, while signalling further tightening ahead."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The dollar held near multi-week highs ahead of the decision, but global bond yields eased after a recent run-up. Germany's 10-year bond yield fell 0.5 basis points to 3.53%, after reaching 3.5723% on Tuesday, its highest level since June 2009."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Central European bond markets followed the global trend in recent days and stabilised on Wednesday, with the Czech 10-year yield at 5.3818% and the Polish at 6.4430%, both unchanged on the day."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Poland's 10-year bond yields had hit a 3-1/2-year high of 6.5530% on Wednesday, before retreating."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The Czech bond market is not immune to the global sell-off. Market interest rates are rising across the domestic yield curve, most notably at the long end. Yesterday, the yield on the 10-year government bond approached 5.4%, the highest level since late 2022,\" Patria Finance Chief Economist Dominik Rusinko said in a note."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The decisive factor will be how long they remain at current levels.\""]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","child